        ///<remarks>The integer return value is the number of colliders that overlap this Collider and which could be stored in the supplied array given its length. The results array will not be resized if it doesn't contain enough elements to report all the results.  The significance of this is that no memory is allocated for the results and so garbage collection performance is improved when the query is performed frequently.</remarks>
